# What we have worked out the language means by some of them.
#
# Ten consecutive shorts hold the formant targets a consonant is spoken with:
# each formant twice, once for the transition into it and once for the one out.
# Read off Italian's own value rules, where the trill sets f1 to 450 and its f2
# to 1250, the labials f2 to 850, the dentals and velars to 1700 and the
# palatals to 1800 -- which is where a labial's low second formant and a
# palatal's high one are supposed to be, so the reading is the language's own.
name short 421 f1_in
name short 422 f1_out
name short 423 f2_in
name short 424 f2_out
name short 425 f3_in
name short 426 f3_out
name short 427 f4_in
name short 428 f4_out
name short 429 f5_in
name short 430 f5_out
